    {
      "id": "blurb",
      "type": "text",
      "position": {
        "x": -900,
        "y": -560
      },
      "size": {
        "width": 900,
        "height": 190
      },
      "style": {
        "fill": "#fefcbf",
        "fontColor": "#744210",
        "fontSize": 12,
        "textAlign": "start",
        "fontFamily": "sans-serif"
      },
      "data": {
        "label": "EXAMPLE — C4 Container: Ticketing & Booking Platform\n\nIllustrates: the second level of the C4 drill-down (Context → Container → Component) — decomposing the system in scope from the Context diagram into its own internal deployable units, using this tool's container/grouping feature (epic 0004) for the system boundary itself.\nPersona: the same technical/solution architect on the modernization task force, one level deeper.\n\nReading this diagram: darker blue = backend services (in scope). Lighter blue = frontend applications (in scope). Teal = the data store (in scope). Purple = human actors (same as Context level). Grey = external/existing systems (same as Context level). The dashed edge is transitional, same convention as the Context diagram.\n\nPart of the Meridian Rail example gallery — epic 0022 (docs/planning/epics/0022-example-diagram-gallery.md). Linked from the Context diagram's \"Ticketing & Booking Platform\" shape."
      }
    },
